## 2. SAP ARCHITECTURE

### 2.1 Three-Tier Architecture (R/3 & ECC)

```
┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│      PRESENTATION LAYER          │
│  (SAP GUI / Web Browser / Fiori) │
└──────────────┬───────────────────┘
               │
┌──────────────▼───────────────────┐
│       APPLICATION LAYER          │
│    (SAP Application Server)      │
│  ┌─────────┐  ┌────────────────┐ │
│  │Dispatcher│  │ Work Processes │ │
│  └─────────┘  │ D  V  B  S  E │ │
│               └────────────────┘ │
└──────────────┬───────────────────┘
               │
┌──────────────▼───────────────────┐
│        DATABASE LAYER            │
│  (Oracle / DB2 / HANA / SQL Srv) │
└──────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 2.2 Work Processes

| Type | Symbol | Function |
|------|--------|----------|
| Dialog | D | Handles user interaction (screen processing) |
| Update | V | Asynchronous database updates |
| Background | B | Scheduled batch jobs |
| Spool | S | Print request processing |
| Enqueue | E | Lock management for data consistency |

### 2.3 SAP Instance Architecture

```
SAP System
├── Central Instance (CI)
│   ├── Message Server (MS) — routes requests between instances
│   ├── Enqueue Server — manages lock table
│   └── ABAP Dispatcher + Work Processes
├── Application Server Instance (AS)
│   └── ABAP Dispatcher + Work Processes
├── Database Instance
│   └── Database Server (Oracle, HANA, etc.)
└── Web Dispatcher (optional)
    └── Load balancing for HTTP/HTTPS requests
```

### 2.4 SAP NetWeaver

SAP NetWeaver is the technology platform that provides the foundation for SAP applications.

**Components:**
- **ABAP Stack**: Runtime for ABAP programs
- **Java Stack**: Runtime for Java applications (Portal, PI/PO)
- **SAP Gateway**: OData services for Fiori apps
- **Process Integration (PI/PO)**: Middleware for system integration
- **Enterprise Portal**: Web-based unified access
- **Business Warehouse (BW)**: Data warehousing and analytics
- **Solution Manager (SolMan)**: Lifecycle management

### 2.5 Memory Management

```
SAP Application Server Memory
├── SAP Extended Memory (EM) — shared memory for all work processes
├── SAP Roll Area — user context storage
├── SAP Paging Area — internal table and extract data
├── Heap Memory — private memory per work process
└── SAP Buffer
    ├── Program Buffer (ABAP code)
    ├── Table Buffer (DDIC table data)
    ├── Nametab Buffer (field catalog)
    └── CUA Buffer (menu/toolbar)
```

