## 6. ABAP PROGRAMMING LANGUAGE

### 6.1 Introduction

**ABAP (Advanced Business Application Programming)** is SAP's proprietary programming language. Originally procedural, it now supports object-oriented programming.

### 6.2 ABAP Program Types

| Type | Code | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| Executable Program | 1 | Standalone report (can be run with SE38) |
| Module Pool | M | Dialog program with screens (SE80) |
| Function Group | F | Container for function modules (SE37) |
| Include | I | Reusable code included in other programs |
| Subroutine Pool | S | Contains FORMs |
| Class Pool | K | Contains global ABAP classes |
| Interface Pool | J | Contains global ABAP interfaces |
| Type Pool | T | Contains global type definitions |

### 6.3 Data Types & Declarations

```abap
" Elementary Data Types
DATA: lv_char    TYPE c LENGTH 10,        " Character (fixed length)
      lv_string  TYPE string,              " Character (variable length)
      lv_int     TYPE i,                   " Integer (4 bytes)
      lv_packed  TYPE p DECIMALS 2,        " Packed number (BCD)
