## 7. SAP HANA

### 7.1 What is SAP HANA?

**SAP HANA (High-performance ANalytic Appliance)** is an in-memory, column-oriented, relational database management system. It processes both OLTP and OLAP workloads in a single system.

### 7.2 Key Features

| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **In-Memory Computing** | All data stored in RAM for ultra-fast access |
| **Column Store** | Data stored column-wise for efficient analytics |
| **Row Store** | Traditional row storage for transactional data |
| **Compression** | Dictionary encoding, run-length, cluster, sparse encoding |
| **Multi-Model** | Graph, spatial, text, document store, time-series |
| **Code Pushdown** | Push data-intensive logic from app server to DB |
| **Real-Time Replication** | SLT, SDA, Smart Data Integration |

### 7.3 Architecture

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    SAP HANA DATABASE                       │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐ │
│  │  Index Server │  │  XS Engine   │  │ Script Server    │ │
│  │ (Core Engine) │  │ (Web Server) │  │ (R/Python/etc.)  │ │
│  │              │  │              │  │                  │ │
│  │ SQL Engine   │  │ OData        │  │ Predictive       │ │
│  │ MDX Engine   │  │ REST API     │  │ Analytics        │ │
│  │ Graph Engine │  │ XSJS/XSODATA │  │ Machine Learning │ │
│  │ Spatial      │  │              │  │                  │ │
│  └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘  └──────────────────┘ │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                    PERSISTENCE LAYER                       │
│            (Data Volumes, Log Volumes, Savepoints)         │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 7.4 Column Store vs Row Store

```
Row Store (Traditional):
┌────────┬────────┬────────┬────────┐
│ ID     │ Name   │ City   │ Salary │ ← Row 1
├────────┼────────┼────────┼────────┤
│ 1      │ Alice  │ NYC    │ 80000  │
│ 2      │ Bob    │ LA     │ 75000  │
│ 3      │ Carol  │ NYC    │ 90000  │
└────────┴────────┴────────┴────────┘

Column Store (HANA):
┌────────┐  ┌────────┐  ┌────────┐  ┌────────┐
│ ID Col │  │Name Col│  │City Col│  │Sal Col │
├────────┤  ├────────┤  ├────────┤  ├────────┤
│ 1      │  │ Alice  │  │ NYC    │  │ 80000  │
│ 2      │  │ Bob    │  │ LA     │  │ 75000  │
│ 3      │  │ Carol  │  │ NYC    │  │ 90000  │
└────────┘  └────────┘  └────────┘  └────────┘

Column Store Advantages:
- SUM(Salary) only reads Salary column (not all columns)
- Better compression (similar values together)
- Parallel processing per column
- Ideal for aggregations and analytics
```

### 7.5 HANA SQL & SQLScript

```sql
-- Basic HANA SQL
SELECT TOP 10 MATNR, MAKTX, MTART
FROM MARA
INNER JOIN MAKT ON MARA.MATNR = MAKT.MATNR
WHERE MAKT.SPRAS = 'E'
ORDER BY MATNR;

-- SQLScript Procedure
CREATE PROCEDURE "SCHEMA"."GET_SALES_SUMMARY" (
    IN iv_year NVARCHAR(4),
    OUT et_result TABLE (
        CUSTOMER NVARCHAR(10),
        TOTAL_AMOUNT DECIMAL(15,2),
        ORDER_COUNT INTEGER
    )
)
LANGUAGE SQLSCRIPT
SQL SECURITY INVOKER
READS SQL DATA
AS
BEGIN
    et_result = SELECT
        KUNNR AS CUSTOMER,
        SUM(NETWR) AS TOTAL_AMOUNT,
        COUNT(*) AS ORDER_COUNT
    FROM VBAK
    WHERE ERDAT LIKE :iv_year || '%'
    GROUP BY KUNNR
    ORDER BY TOTAL_AMOUNT DESC;
END;

-- Table Function
CREATE FUNCTION "SCHEMA"."TF_TOP_MATERIALS" (iv_count INTEGER)
RETURNS TABLE (
    MATNR NVARCHAR(18),
    TOTAL_QTY DECIMAL(13,3)
)
LANGUAGE SQLSCRIPT
READS SQL DATA
AS
BEGIN
    RETURN SELECT TOP :iv_count
        MATNR,
        SUM(MENGE) AS TOTAL_QTY
    FROM MSEG
    GROUP BY MATNR
    ORDER BY TOTAL_QTY DESC;
END;
```

