## 16. SAP BEST PRACTICES

### 16.1 ABAP Development Best Practices

| Practice | Details |
|----------|---------|
| **Naming Convention** | Z/Y prefix for custom objects (ZREPORT, ZTABLE, ZCL_CLASS) |
| **Avoid SELECT *** | Always specify required fields explicitly |
| **Use FOR ALL ENTRIES** | Instead of SELECT inside LOOP. Check IF table IS NOT INITIAL first |
| **Index Usage** | Ensure WHERE clause fields have database indexes |
| **Internal Table Types** | Use SORTED/HASHED for key-based access, STANDARD for append-only |
| **Field Symbols** | Use ASSIGNING instead of INTO for better performance |
| **Binary Search** | Use BINARY SEARCH with READ TABLE on sorted internal tables |
| **Code Inspector** | Run SCI/ATC before transport |
| **Error Handling** | Use exceptions, check sy-subrc after every operation |
| **Modularization** | Use classes/methods over subroutines (FORMs) |
| **AMDP** | Push data-intensive logic to HANA (code pushdown) |

### 16.2 Performance Optimization

```
ABAP Performance Checklist:
├── Database Level
│   ├── Minimize round-trips (use JOINs, FOR ALL ENTRIES)
│   ├── Use appropriate indexes
│   ├── Avoid nested SELECTs
│   └── Use HANA code pushdown (CDS, AMDP)
├── Application Level
│   ├── Use HASHED tables for lookups
│   ├── Use FIELD-SYMBOLS for table operations
│   ├── Avoid unnecessary data copies
│   ├── Buffer master data reads
